cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, with the version you used."
type: software
title: "EIS Analysis Toolkit (eis_analysis)"
abstract: >-
  A command-line tool for electrochemical impedance spectroscopy that
  reads Gamry DTA and CSV files: Kramers-Kronig validation (Lin-KK,
  Z-HIT), distribution of relaxation times with automatic regularization
  and peak detection, R_inf estimation, equivalent-circuit fitting by
  differential evolution or multistart with model comparison (AIC/BIC), a
  model-free map of the local CPE exponent, and
  oxide-layer analysis (thickness, permittivity). The same functions are
  available as a Python library.
authors:
  - family-names: Chmela
    given-names: Tomáš
    affiliation: "UJP PRAHA"
    email: chmela@ujp.cz
repository-code: "https://github.com/chmelat/eis_analysis"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - electrochemical impedance spectroscopy
  - distribution of relaxation times
  - Kramers-Kronig
  - equivalent circuit fitting
  - differential evolution
